INT. BOXING GYM - LOCKER ROOM - NIGHT

Steam. Rusted lockers. A bare bulb swings from a chain. The smell of liniment and old leather.

MANUEL "THE ANVIL" SERRANO, 30s, sits on a bench with gloved hands in his lap, staring at the floor. His trainer, IGNATIUS OBI-MARTINEZ, 60s, kneels in front of him, taping a wrist with absent care.

A TALL MAN in a camel coat leans in the doorway. No one introduced him. He has been watching for a while.

                    IGNATIUS
Stay loose.

Manuel nods. His eyes do not leave the floor.

                    IGNATIUS (CONT'D)
Breathe through the nose.

Manuel breathes. Ignatius tears the tape with his teeth.

The Tall Man clears his throat.

                    TALL MAN
Mr. Serrano.

Manuel doesn't look up. Ignatius's hands stop.

                    TALL MAN (CONT'D)
My name is Ambrose Vance. I represent the promoter.

                    IGNATIUS
He's got a fight.

                    AMBROSE
I'm aware.

                    IGNATIUS
So you can wait outside.

                    AMBROSE
I can't.

The bulb swings. Manuel's shadow slides across the lockers. Ignatius rises, one knee cracking, and plants himself between them.

                    IGNATIUS
Say what you came to say.

                    AMBROSE
It's about the third round.

Ignatius and Manuel both go still. The steam hisses from a pipe.

                    AMBROSE (CONT'D)
Mr. Serrano goes down in the third. The money is already placed.

                    IGNATIUS
^
Get out.

                    MANUEL
^
Get out.

They say it at the same time, quiet and level. Ambrose lifts both hands, palms out, and steps back through the doorway into the corridor.

Ignatius shuts the door. Leans against it with his eyes closed. Manuel finally lifts his head. His gloved hands, slowly, curl into fists.
